  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1239 AM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge over the southeastern U.S. will continue  \nto expand westward into our area from Thursday through the first \npart of the weekend. The ridge will not be quite as strong as it \nhas been over the last week, but temperatures will still be well \nabove normal- in the mid 90s to near 101 degrees Thursday through \nSaturday. A pattern shift then looks to commence late in the \nweekend into early next week. An upper level trough is forecast to\ndeepen over the Rockies and then move eastward into the northern \nand Central Plains. This may help to temporarily weaken the ridge \nand send a frontal boundary into north Texas. Model blends \ncontinue to advertise rain chances Sunday evening into Monday and \nTuesday, but there is still uncertainty regarding coverage and \namounts. Highs are forecast to be above average on Monday and \nTuesday -lower to mid 90s on Monday and lower 90s on Tuesday.",
